================================================================================
What this package contains, and who wrote it
================================================================================

Unbake was extracted from an unofficial fork of ComfyUI-Lora-Manager (GPL-3.0).
That is unusual enough to state precisely, because "extracted from a GPL fork"
can mean two very different things.

  * All but ONE source file here was written by this package's author. Those
    files do not exist upstream, and no six consecutive lines of them match
    upstream text.

  * ONE file is upstream's and is redistributed unchanged:

        web/core/genParamsMapper.js      (ComfyUI-Lora-Manager, GPL-3.0)

    It maps A1111 sampler/scheduler display names onto ComfyUI's internal
    values. Keeping it is a deliberate choice: this package is distributed
    free of charge under GPL-3.0, so there is nothing to gain by rewriting it,
    and GPL is the licence that keeps someone else from folding this work into
    a closed paid product.

The file list is not repeated here in prose. A list written into a document is
a copy of a fact that lives in the tree, and it goes stale the first time a
file is added. `tests/source_integrity_test.mjs` reads the tree instead, and
`UPSTREAM_FILES` in that test is the single place the exception is declared.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
How to verify the separation yourself
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Do not take any of the above on trust. All of it is mechanically checkable.

  1. Confirm nothing reaches outside this package:

       grep -rn "^import\|^export.*from\|from '\|require(" web/

     Every specifier resolves to a sibling inside `web/`. Nothing points at
     `comfyui-lora-manager`, at `../../..`, or at an npm package.

     The Python side is checked the same way:

       python -c "import ast,pathlib;print(sorted({(('.'*n.level)+(n.module or '')) if isinstance(n,ast.ImportFrom) else a.name for p in pathlib.Path('unbake').rglob('*.py') for n in ast.walk(ast.parse(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'))) if isinstance(n,(ast.Import,ast.ImportFrom)) for a in (n.names if isinstance(n,ast.Import) else [None]) if True}))"

     Everything printed is a Python standard-library module, a sibling inside
     `unbake`, `folder_paths` (supplied by ComfyUI itself), or `PIL` (shipped
     with ComfyUI, imported lazily inside the two functions that read PNG
     metadata).

  2. Confirm the analysis core never reaches the network on its own:

       node --test tests/source_integrity_test.mjs

     `web/core/` contains zero references to the global `fetch` identifier.
     The one place that talks to ComfyUI is `web/host/comfyHost.js`, and the
     core reaches it only through the environment it is handed.

     This mattered before extraction: `/object_info` was fetched from inside
     the capability module, which is precisely what tied the analysis to the
     fork's own web page. The boundary is now held by a test rather than by a
     sentence in a README.

  3. Confirm the author's files are not upstream text under a new name:

       node tests/upstream_copy_scan.mjs --upstream <path-to-upstream-checkout>

     This indexes every six-line block of an upstream checkout (whitespace
     normalised, comments removed) and reports any match.

     Run it with a control. The scan is only meaningful if it can fire, and a
     result of zero is otherwise indistinguishable from a broken scanner.
     `web/core/genParamsMapper.js` is upstream's file and is therefore the
     control: it must report matches. When this was measured against upstream
     v1.1.6 and v1.1.9, the author's files reported 0 blocks and the control
     reported hundreds.

     Get an upstream checkout with:

       gh api repos/willmiao/ComfyUI-Lora-Manager/tarball/v1.1.9 > upstream.tar.gz

  4. Confirm the copyright notices are complete:

       node --test tests/source_integrity_test.mjs

     Every file the author wrote carries `Copyright (C) 2026 syugoji`, and the
     upstream file does not. This is the only thing that keeps a different
     licence available later; a file distributed without a notice is harder to
     claim afterwards.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Relationship to genrecord
================================================================================

`genrecord` (AGPL-3.0 + commercial) shares this project's vocabulary — it also
speaks of a Generation Record — and shares none of its code. The two do
different jobs and the split is intentional:

    genrecord   decides whether a record could be reproduced. It never runs
                anything, has no dependencies, and is deterministic.
    Unbake      builds the graph and runs it, then sweeps parameters and puts
                the results side by side.

Neither imports the other. If you want the judgement without the runtime, take
genrecord; if you want the workbench, take this.

================================================================================
Third-party material
================================================================================

  ComfyUI-Lora-Manager (GPL-3.0) — `web/core/genParamsMapper.js`, unchanged.
    https://github.com/willmiao/ComfyUI-Lora-Manager

Nothing else. This package bundles no npm dependency and no Python dependency;
`folder_paths` and `PIL` come from the ComfyUI installation it runs inside.

No licence data obtained from any distributor is included.

A small built-in catalogue IS included: `unbake/services/known_model_catalog.py`
lists 26 upscaler and auxiliary models by filename, alias, and download URL. It
exists because A1111 and ComfyUI name the same file differently (for example
"R-ESRGAN 4x+ Anime6B" is `RealESRGAN_x4plus_anime_6B.pth`), and without the
alias table a model that is already installed reads as missing. The entries are
names and public URLs written by this project; no model weights and no
distributor data are bundled. Callers may supply a different catalogue at
runtime, and the code works with an empty one.
